 average of the maximum and minimum values. \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}_{\\text{min}}+{y}_{\\text{max}}}{2} & =\\frac{- \\frac{89}{6}+\\frac{19}{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{-89}{6}+\\frac{57}{6}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{- \\frac{16}{3}}{2} \\\\  & =- \\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the midline is $y=- \\frac{8}{3}.$" 13194139535796 17592186045443 true] [17592186528249 1068 #edb/ref 17592186528293 13194139535796 17592186045443 true] [17592186528249 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535796 17592186045443 true] [17592186528249 1071 "Find the equation of the midline for a transformed sine function with a minimum value of $-5$ and a maximum value of $4.$" 13194139535796 17592186045443 true] [17592186528249 1072 #uuid "90faa74d-85c8-5992-b843-f857e8de677b" 13194139535796 17592186045443 true] [17592186528249 1074 "A sinusoidal graph's midline (or vertical shift) is the horizontal line that divides it vertically in half. \n\nThe equation of the midline is given by\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{{y}_{\\text{min}}+{y}_{\\text{max}}}{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{\\text{min}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{max}}$ are the minimum and maximum values of the function. The midline equals the average of the maximum and minimum values. \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}_{\\text{min}}+{y}_{\\text{max}}}{2} & =\\frac{-5+4}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{2} \\\\  & =- \\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the midline is $y=- \\frac{1}{2}.$" 13194139535796 17592186045443 true] [17592186528250 1080 "y=- \\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535796 17592186045443 true] [17592186528250 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535796 17592186045443 true] [17592186528250 1083 #uuid "92b45187-9e0c-55b3-aaa3-5df7bd1882ce" 13194139535796 17592186045443 true] [17592186528251 1080 "y=-14" 13194139535796 17592186045443 true] [17592186528251 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535796 17592186045443 true] [17592186528251 1083 #uuid "93b9e714-df26-5d8c-bc9b-266c87d2634b" 13194139535796 